        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Sealing a driveway is a job where the result depends almost entirely on preparation and weather, not on how much material you spread. Clean it properly, fill every crack wider than a pencil line, wait for a dry surface and a dry forecast, and lay down two thin coats instead of one thick one.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Do that and a homeowner can match contractor results for a fraction of the cost, then repeat the job every two to three years rather than every spring. If you have not picked a product yet, start with our ranked list of asphalt sealers and buy one more pail than the math says you need.
          </p>
